---
import DocsLayout from '../../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro'
---
<DocsLayout title="Arrows Plugin">
  <h1>Arrows</h1>
  <p class="lead">Injects previous and next navigation buttons into the slider's outer wrapper. Buttons are automatically disabled at the first and last slide when <code>loop</code> and <code>rewind</code> are both off.</p>

  <h2>Import</h2>
  <pre><code>import {"{"} arrows {"}"} from '@andresclua/sliderkit-plugins'</code></pre>

  <h2>Options</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Option</th><th>Type</th><th>Default</th><th>Description</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>prevText</code></td><td>string</td><td>chevron SVG</td><td>innerHTML of the prev button. The <code>aria-label</code> is always "Previous slide".</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>nextText</code></td><td>string</td><td>chevron SVG</td><td>innerHTML of the next button. The <code>aria-label</code> is always "Next slide".</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>container</code></td><td>HTMLElement | string | null</td><td>outer wrapper</td><td>Where to append the buttons.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>wrapper</code></td><td>boolean</td><td><code>true</code></td><td>Wrap both buttons in a <code>.sliderkit__arrows</code> div. Set to <code>false</code> to append them directly.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>CSS classes</h2>
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Class</th><th>Applied when</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>.sliderkit__arrow</code></td><td>Both buttons, always.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>.sliderkit__arrows</code></td><td>Wrapper around both buttons (unless <code>wrapper: false</code>).</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>.sliderkit__arrow--prev</code></td><td>Previous button.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>.sliderkit__arrow--next</code></td><td>Next button.</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>.sliderkit__arrow--disabled</code></td><td>At the first or last slide when <code>loop:false</code> and <code>rewind:false</code>.</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2>Example</h2>
  <pre><code>import {"{"} Slider {"}"} from '@andresclua/sliderkit'
import {"{"} arrows {"}"} from '@andresclua/sliderkit-plugins'

new Slider('#my-slider', {"{"}
  items: 1,
  loop:  true,
  plugins: [arrows()],
{"}"})</code></pre>

  <h2>Custom button content</h2>
  <pre><code>arrows({"{"}
  prevText: '←',
  nextText: '→',
{"}"})</code></pre>

  <p>The arrows are hidden automatically when all slides fit in the viewport (<code>slideCount &lt;= items</code>), and re-evaluated on every breakpoint change.</p>

  <p><a href="/demos/base">See it live in the Base demo →</a></p>
</DocsLayout>
